              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "CDIAL lists ਕੰਧ (kandh), \"wall\", under Sanskrit kanthā, \"wall, town\", which it takes from Iranian (CDIAL 2720). It adds that the word coincides with kaṇṭha, \"throat; border\", under which it lists Punjabi kaṇḍh, \"wall\" (CDIAL 2680)."
